<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30306" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mystĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυστικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to secret rites</i> or <i>mysteries, mystic, mystical</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mystica sacra Dindymenes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					8, 81, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vannus Iacchi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 166</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					3, 6, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lampas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 8, 765</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mystĭ-ca</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., <i>things pertaining to secret rites</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Lampr. Alex. Sev. 26</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			2353</span></i>.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mystĭcē</span></b> , <i>mystically</i> (post-class.), <i><span class="en">Sol.
			32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Luc. 7, §
			9</span></i>.</div>
